<reference id="AddandEditExportObjectsWindow-540E5726" xml:lang="en" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">New (and Edit) export objects window</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">This window prepares components for export to BACnet objects.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">objects export</indexterm><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">New window<indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">for object export</indexterm></indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section ">
            <fig id="ID-fig-0000000b" class="- topic/fig "><title id="ID-0000025f" class="- topic/title ">New window in Bacnet Export Manager</title><image placement="break" scale="65" scope="local" href="../graphic/ServerExportMgrAddDialog1RO_0000045139.png" class="- topic/image "/></fig>
            <p class="- topic/p ">This window opens when you expand <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetNetwork</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetDevice</uicontrol></menucascade>, double-click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">ExportFolder</uicontrol> and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">New</uicontrol> or select a row and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Edit</uicontrol> in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Bacnet Export Manager</wintitle>.</p>
            <p class="- topic/p ">All properties in this window apply separately to each highlighted (for export) component.</p>
            <note type="note" class="- topic/note ">
                <p class="- topic/p ">Select <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Type</parmname> first before entering other properties, such as <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Object Name</parmname> and <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Description</parmname>. Entering type clears the other properties and you will need to enter them again. <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Type</parmname> is the only property you cannot change after adding an export descriptor.</p>
            </note>
        </section><properties class="- topic/simpletable reference/properties "><prophead class="- topic/sthead      reference/prophead "><proptypehd class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptypehd ">Property</proptypehd><propvaluehd class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvaluehd ">Value</propvaluehd><propdeschd class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdeschd ">Description</propdeschd></prophead><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Name</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">read-only</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">
                    <div conref="../reuse/WH-guide-BACnet.dita#WH-guide-BACnet-0ED816BF/bacnetName-div" class="- topic/div "/>
                </propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Object Name</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">read-only</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">
                    <div conref="../reuse/WH-guide-BACnet.dita#WH-guide-BACnet-0ED816BF/bacnetObjectName-div" class="- topic/div "/>
                    <p class="- topic/p ">In an export folder this is the name for the SVO (Structured View Object) that the export folder represents. This name must be unique at this level in the structured view hierarchy.</p>
